# Dev default: empty backend URL => the client uses same-origin relative URLs,
# which Vite's dev server proxies to the backend (see `server.proxy` in
# vite.config.mts). Benefits: no CORS in dev, and the app is reachable over the
# LAN via the frontend port alone (http://<your-ip>:4200) with no second open
# port. Override per-machine in an untracked .env.local if needed; production
# builds (mode=production) ignore this file and fall back to the localhost
# default in config.ts unless VITE_BLOOM_BACKEND_URL is set.
VITE_BLOOM_BACKEND_URL=
